course: dictionary
lesson: 12943
title: Exceed: going beyond
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To exceed something means to go beyond it: to be more than a number or amount, or to go past a limit or rule. «The bag must not exceed 20 kilograms» means it can weigh 20 kilograms, but it must not go over.
explain: Exceed is a verb: exceed, exceeds, exceeded, exceeding. «The number 60 exceeds 50» means 60 is more than 50. Exceed does not mean equal, so 50 does not exceed 50.
explain: Exceed can also mean doing better than people expected. «Her drawing exceeded everyone's expectations» means it was far better than anyone thought it would be.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. A limit, a number or a rule tells you that exceed means going over it. Swap in "went over" or "was more than" to check that your meaning still makes sense.
fact: Exceed means to be more than a number or amount.
fact: Exceed also means to go beyond a limit or rule that is allowed.
fact: «Speed must not exceed 30 mph» means the car can go up to 30 mph, but not faster.
fact: In maths, «exceeds 50» means is more than 50, not equal to 50.
fact: The phrases «exceed the limit» and «exceed expectations» are useful to remember.
exercise: «Speed must not exceed 30 mph.» What does exceed mean here? | Forget about | Stay exactly on | Slow down below | *Go over
exercise: «The number 80 exceeds 50.» Is 80 less than, equal to or more than 50? | Less than | *More than | Exactly the same as 50 | Equal to
exercise: «Her score exceeded our expectations.» What does this tell you? | Her score was lower than we hoped | *Her score was better than we expected | We forgot her score | Her score was the same as always
test: «The baker must not exceed 100 cakes a day.» What does exceed mean in this sentence? | Match | Be less than | Stay exactly at | *Go beyond
test: Which phrase means "did much better than people thought"? | Was equal to | Fell short | Met the limit exactly | *Exceeded expectations
exam: Maya says, «The total exceeds 40.» Which number could be the total? | 40 | 39 | *41 | 38
